{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hotheaded-dutiable-addax","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Found by comparing rebar's DC adapter against mature OSS Jira integrations.\n\n## What is SOLIDLY established\n\n* A Jira issue's KEY changes when it is moved between projects; its numeric `id` NEVER does.\n* Old keys are stacked in the `moved_issue_key` table so the old key normally still resolves.\n* Per an Atlassian **Data-Center-specific** KB, third-party apps that move issues via workflow\n  post-functions, automations, or scheduled routines can FAIL to update that table — after which the\n  old key simply stops resolving.\n\nrebar's bindings are keyed on the Jira KEY. So a moved issue can silently detach.\n\n## What is NOT established — do not build on it yet\n\nAn earlier pass of this research asserted that `GET /rest/api/2/issue/{oldKey}` returns HTTP 200 with a\nbody carrying the NEW key. **That was not verifiable** — the Atlassian KB does not state what the\nendpoint returns for a stale key (200-with-new-key vs 301 vs 404), and the researching agent\nexplicitly retracted the claim on a second pass.\n\n**Confirm empirically against the 8.17.1 harness before writing detection code.** The remediation\nbelow stands regardless; only the DETECTION mechanism is unverified.\n\n## Remediation\n\nKey bindings on the numeric `id` rather than the `key`, keeping the key as a display/convenience\nfield. That is invariant under project moves and needs no detection heuristic at all.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the harness establishes what GET on a moved issue's OLD key actually\n      returns on DC 8.17.1 — recorded as evidence, since two research passes disagreed\n- [ ] bindings resolve an issue by numeric `id`, so a project move does not detach the binding\n- [ ] a test moves (or simulates moving) an issue and asserts the binding survives\n- [ ] the `key` remains available for display and for JQL, but is not the identity","id":"7c26-4ac8-04a3-440e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bindings key on the Jira KEY, which changes when an issue moves project"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785497187723216001,"uuid":"13f1b0ac-82f2-485b-bce3-732752912898"}